{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BGusWBC6kAiqvaHWiW4JcS","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: prd020-true\n     2→title: \"cmd/true: Exit Successfully\"\n     3→\n     4→problem: |\n     5→  Shell scripts use true as a no-op command that always succeeds. It appears in conditional\n     6→  expressions, while loops (while true; do ...; done), and as a placeholder in pipelines.\n     7→  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gtrue, installed by\n     8→  coreutils) in exit code behavior and output, verified by differential testing via\n     9→  pkg/testutils under LC_ALL=C.\n    10→\n    11→goals:\n    12→  - G1: Exit with status 0 unconditionally, matching GNU true exit behavior.\n    13→  - G2: Handle --help and --version flags, matching GNU true flag handling.\n    14→\n    15→requirements:\n    16→  R1:\n    17→    title: Exit status\n    18→    items:\n    19→      - R1.1: Must exit with status 0 when invoked with no arguments.\n    20→      - R1.2: Must exit with status 0 when invoked with any arguments that are not --help or --version. Arguments are not parsed, validated, or acted upon; they are silently ignored.\n    21→      - R1.3: Must not read from stdin under any circumstances.\n    22→      - R1.4: Must not write to stdout or stderr under normal operation (no arguments or unrecognized arguments).\n    23→\n    24→  R2:\n    25→    title: Flag handling (--help, --version)\n    26→    items:\n    27→      - R2.1: When --help is the first argument, must print a usage message to stdout and exit 0. Remaining arguments after --help are ignored.\n    28→      - R2.2: When --version is the first argument, must print version information to stdout and exit 0. Remaining arguments after --version are ignored.\n    29→      - R2.3: Only the first argument is checked for --help and --version. If --help or --version appears in any position other than the first argument, it is ignored and true exits 0 silently.\n    30→\n    31→  R3:\n    32→    title: Operand behavior\n    33→    items:\n    34→      - R3.1: All operands (non-flag arguments) are silently ignored. true does not distinguish between flags and operands; everything except --help and --version as the first argument is discarded.\n    35→      - R3.2: The \"--\" end-of-options marker has no special meaning to true. It is ignored like any other argument.\n    36→\n    37→  R4:\n    38→    title: SIGPIPE handling\n    39→    items:\n    40→      - R4.1: |\n    41→          Must install a SIGPIPE handler at startup using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler, matching\n    42→          the pattern used by other utilities in the project (see cmd/cat/main.go). This ensures\n    43→          silent exit when stdout is closed by a downstream consumer in a pipeline.\n    44→\n    45→  R5:\n    46→    title: Error handling and exit codes\n    47→    items:\n    48→      - R5.1: Must exit 0 in all cases except a write error during --help or --version output.\n    49→      - R5.2: If a write error occurs while printing --help or --version output (e.g., SIGPIPE or full disk), must exit 1.\n    50→      - R5.3: \"Error messages for write failures must be written to stderr in the format: \\\"true: <error description>\\\".\"\n    51→      - R5.4: Must not exit with any status other than 0 or 1.\n    52→\n    53→non_goals:\n    54→  - cmd/true does not implement any flags beyond --help and --version.\n    55→  - cmd/true does not perform any computation or I/O beyond the optional help/version output.\n    56→  - cmd/true does not read from stdin or process piped input.\n    57→\n    58→acceptance_criteria:\n    59→  - \"AC1: go run ./cmd/true; echo $? prints 0.\"\n    60→  - \"AC2: go run ./cmd/true foo bar --baz; echo $? prints 0.\"\n    61→  - \"AC3: go run ./cmd/true --help prints a usage message to stdout and exits 0.\"\n    62→  - \"AC4: go run ./cmd/true --version prints version information to stdout and exits 0.\"\n    63→  - \"AC5: Differential test against gtrue passes with LC_ALL=C for no-args, arbitrary-args, and single-unrecognized-flag cases, comparing exit codes.\"\n    64→  - \"AC6: Differential test verifies no stdout or stderr output when invoked without --help or --version, under LC_ALL=C.\"\n    65→  - \"AC7: cmd/true compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    66→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c1506a9-03c5-4381-b2d8-e6c523aa04b7","uuid":"c29f09cc-8e01-456b-9c93-e97e536cff1d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/204/docs/specs/product-requirements/prd020-true.yaml","content":"id: prd020-true\ntitle: \"cmd/true: Exit Successfully\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Shell scripts use true as a no-op command that always succeeds. It appears in conditional\n  expressions, while loops (while true; do ...; done), and as a placeholder in pipelines.\n  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gtrue, installed by\n  coreutils) in exit code behavior and output, verified by differential testing via\n  pkg/testutils under LC_ALL=C.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Exit with status 0 unconditionally, matching GNU true exit behavior.\n  - G2: Handle --help and --version flags, matching GNU true flag handling.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Exit status\n    items:\n      - R1.1: Must exit with status 0 when invoked with no arguments.\n      - R1.2: Must exit with status 0 when invoked with any arguments that are not --help or --version. Arguments are not parsed, validated, or acted upon; they are silently ignored.\n      - R1.3: Must not read from stdin under any circumstances.\n      - R1.4: Must not write to stdout or stderr under normal operation (no arguments or unrecognized arguments).\n\n  R2:\n    title: Flag handling (--help, --version)\n    items:\n      - R2.1: When --help is the first argument, must print a usage message to stdout and exit 0. Remaining arguments after --help are ignored.\n      - R2.2: When --version is the first argument, must print version information to stdout and exit 0. Remaining arguments after --version are ignored.\n      - R2.3: Only the first argument is checked for --help and --version. If --help or --version appears in any position other than the first argument, it is ignored and true exits 0 silently.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Operand behavior\n    items:\n      - R3.1: All operands (non-flag arguments) are silently ignored. true does not distinguish between flags and operands; everything except --help and --version as the first argument is discarded.\n      - R3.2: The \"--\" end-of-options marker has no special meaning to true. It is ignored like any other argument.\n\n  R4:\n    title: SIGPIPE handling\n    items:\n      - R4.1: |\n          Must install a SIGPIPE handler at startup using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler, matching\n          the pattern used by other utilities in the project (see cmd/cat/main.go). This ensures\n          silent exit when stdout is closed by a downstream consumer in a pipeline.\n\n  R5:\n    title: Error handling and exit codes\n    items:\n      - R5.1: Must exit 0 in all cases except a write error during --help or --version output.\n      - R5.2: If a write error occurs while printing --help or --version output (e.g., SIGPIPE or full disk), must exit 1.\n      - R5.3: \"Error messages for write failures must be written to stderr in the format: \\\"true: <error description>\\\".\"\n      - R5.4: Must not exit with any status other than 0 or 1.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/true does not implement any flags beyond --help and --version.\n  - cmd/true does not perform any computation or I/O beyond the optional help/version output.\n  - cmd/true does not read from stdin or process piped input.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - \"AC1: go run ./cmd/true; echo $? prints 0.\"\n  - \"AC2: go run ./cmd/true foo bar --baz; echo $? prints 0.\"\n  - \"AC3: go run ./cmd/true --help prints a usage message to stdout and exits 0.\"\n  - \"AC4: go run ./cmd/true --version prints version information to stdout and exits 0.\"\n  - \"AC5: Differential test against gtrue passes with LC_ALL=C for no-args, arbitrary-args, and single-unrecognized-flag cases, comparing exit codes.\"\n  - \"AC6: Differential test verifies no stdout or stderr output when invoked without --help or --version, under LC_ALL=C.\"\n  - \"AC7: cmd/true compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XbiDqmXBdeXT1acUZHCg2D","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     2→// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     3→\n     4→// cmd/true exits with status 0 unconditionally. It silently ignores all\n     5→// arguments except --help and --version as the first argument. Matches\n     6→// GNU coreutils true behavior under LC_ALL=C.\n     7→//\n     8→// Implements prd020-true R1-R5.\n     9→package main\n    10→\n    11→import (\n    12→\t\"bufio\"\n    13→\t\"fmt\"\n    14→\t\"os\"\n    15→\n    16→\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n    17→)\n    18→\n    19→const progName = \"true\"\n    20→\n    21→// version is set at build time via -ldflags \"-X main.version=<tag>\".\n    22→var version = \"dev\"\n    23→\n    24→func main() {\n    25→\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n    26→\n    27→\targs := os.Args[1:]\n    28→\n    29→\t// No arguments: exit 0 silently (R1.1).\n    30→\tif len(args) == 0 {\n    31→\t\tos.Exit(0)\n    32→\t}\n    33→\n    34→\t// Only the first argument is checked for --help and --version (R2.3).\n    35→\tswitch args[0] {\n    36→\tcase \"--help\":\n    37→\t\tprintHelp()\n    38→\tcase \"--version\":\n    39→\t\tprintVersion()\n    40→\t}\n    41→\n    42→\t// All other arguments are silently ignored (R1.2, R3.1, R3.2).\n    43→\tos.Exit(0)\n    44→}\n    45→\n    46→// printHelp writes a usage message to stdout and exits 0 (R2.1).\n    47→// On write error, exits 1 with a diagnostic on stderr (R5.2, R5.3).\n    48→func printHelp() {\n    49→\tout := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n    50→\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \"Usage: %s [ignored command line arguments]\\n\", progName)\n    51→\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \"  or:  %s OPTION\\n\", progName)\n    52→\tfmt.Fprintln(out, \"Exit with a status code indicating success.\")\n    53→\tfmt.Fprintln(out)\n    54→\tfmt.Fprintln(out, \"      --help     display this help and exit\")\n    55→\tfmt.Fprintln(out, \"      --version  output version information and exit\")\n    56→\n    57→\tif err := out.Flush(); err != nil {\n    58→\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"%s: %v\\n\", progName, err)\n    59→\t\tos.Exit(1)\n    60→\t}\n    61→\n    62→\tos.Exit(0)\n    63→}\n    64→\n    65→// printVersion writes version information to stdout and exits 0 (R2.2).\n    66→// On write error, exits 1 with a diagnostic on stderr (R5.2, R5.3).\n    67→func printVersion() {\n    68→\tout := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n    69→\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \"%s (%s) %s\\n\", progName, \"go-unix-utils\", version)\n    70→\n    71→\tif err := out.Flush(); err != nil {\n    72→\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"%s: %v\\n\", progName, err)\n    73→\t\tos.Exit(1)\n    74→\t}\n    75→\n    76→\tos.Exit(0)\n    77→}\n    78→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c1506a9-03c5-4381-b2d8-e6c523aa04b7","uuid":"6fedaee9-20da-4424-af4d-4d0c3ded0032","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/204/cmd/true/main.go","content":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// cmd/true exits with status 0 unconditionally. It silently ignores all\n// arguments except --help and --version as the first argument. Matches\n// GNU coreutils true behavior under LC_ALL=C.\n//\n// Implements prd020-true R1-R5.\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n\nconst progName = \"true\"\n\n// version is set at build time via -ldflags \"-X main.version=<tag>\".\nvar version = \"dev\"\n\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n\targs := os.Args[1:]\n\n\t// No arguments: exit 0 silently (R1.1).\n\tif len(args) == 0 {\n\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t}\n\n\t// Only the first argument is checked for --help and --version (R2.3).\n\tswitch args[0] {\n\tcase \"--help\":\n\t\tprintHelp()\n\tcase \"--version\":\n\t\tprintVersion()\n\t}\n\n\t// All other arguments are silently ignored (R1.2, R3.1, R3.2).\n\tos.Exit(0)\n}\n\n// printHelp writes a usage message to stdout and exits 0 (R2.1).\n// On write error, exits 1 with a diagnostic on stderr (R5.2, R5.3).\nfunc printHelp() {\n\tout := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \"Usage: %s [ignored command line arguments]\\n\", progName)\n\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \"  or:  %s OPTION\\n\", progName)\n\tfmt.Fprintln(out, \"Exit with a status code indicating success.\")\n\tfmt.Fprintln(out)\n\tfmt.Fprintln(out, \"      --help     display this help and exit\")\n\tfmt.Fprintln(out, \"      --version  output version information and exit\")\n\n\tif err := out.Flush(); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"%s: %v\\n\", progName, err)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\n\tos.Exit(0)\n}\n\n// printVersion writes version information to stdout and exits 0 (R2.2).\n// On write error, exits 1 with a diagnostic on stderr (R5.2, R5.3).\nfunc printVersion() {\n\tout := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n\tfmt.Fprintf(out, \"%s (%s) %s\\n\", progName, \"go-unix-utils\", version)\n\n\tif err := out.Flush(); err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"%s: %v\\n\", progName, err)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\n\tos.Exit(0)\n}\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
